                    "a": "Jacobabad — Sardar Sher Muhammad Bijarani (politician and former minister from Jacobabad, worked for the people of his district).\nKashmore / Kandhkot — Mir Hazar Khan Bijarani (politician and former minister from Kashmore, worked for the people of his district).\nShikarpur — Allah Bakhsh Soomro (born in Shikarpur, former Premier of Sindh).\nGhotki — Sardar Ali Mohammad Mahar (former Chief Minister of Sindh, from Ghotki).\nKamber / Shahdadkot — Nawabzada Mir Nadir Ali Khan Magsi (politician from Kamber Shahdadkot, worked for the people of his district).\nLarkana — Hyder Bakhsh Jatoi (born in a small village in Larkana district in 1901; worked hard for the farmers of Sindh and the Sindh Tenancy Act was passed in 1950 because of his work).\nSukkur — Syed Khursheed Ahmed Shah (politician from Sukkur, former Leader of the Opposition in the National Assembly).\nDadu — Allama I.I. Qazi (born on 19th April, 1886 in the village of Pat Sharif in Dadu; first head of Sindh University).\nNaushahro Feroze — Ghulam Mustafa Jatoi (former caretaker Prime Minister of Pakistan, from Naushahro Feroze).\nKhairpur — Hazrat Sachal Sarmast (born in 1739 in the village of Daraza, Khairpur; the Sufi poet known as 'Shair-e-Haft Zaban').\nShaheed Benazirabad — Hakim Ali Zardari (politician from Nawabshah, worked for the people of his district).\nSanghar — Jam Madad Ali Khan (politician from Sanghar, former minister, worked for the people of his district).\nJamshoro — Lal Shahbaz Qalandar (the great Sufi saint whose shrine is at Sehwan Sharif in Jamshoro district).\nMatiari — Shah Abdul Latif Bhittai (the great Sufi poet of Sindh, lived at Bhit Shah in Matiari district).\nHyderabad — Mirza Qaleech Baig (born in Hyderabad in 1853; the great Sindhi writer known as the father of modern Sindhi literature).\nTando Allahyar — Syed Ali Nawaz Shah (politician from Tando Allahyar, worked for the people of his district).\nTando Muhammad Khan — Syed Naveed Qamar (politician from Tando Muhammad Khan, former federal minister).\nMirpurkhas — Nawab Muhammad Yousuf Talpur (politician from Mirpurkhas, worked for the people of his district).\nUmerkot — Rana Chandra Singh (politician from Umerkot, worked for the people of his district).\nTharparkar — Arbab Ghulam Rahim (former Chief Minister of Sindh, from Tharparkar).\nKarachi — Benazir Bhutto (born on 21 June 1953 in Karachi; the first woman elected to lead a Muslim state and the first female Prime Minister of Pakistan).\nThatta — Sassui Palijo (politician from Jungshahi, Thatta; former minister, worked for the people of her district).\nSijawal — Muhammad Ali Malkani (politician from Sijawal, former minister, worked for the people of his district).\nBadin — Dr. Zulfiqar Ali Mirza (politician from Badin, former Home Minister of Sindh).",
